      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُوَّاقٌ</span></b>  <i>Long in the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاق</span> [or <i>shank</i>]. (AA, K.
[See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْوَقُ</span>.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And (assumed tropical:)  <i>Having a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاق</span> [or
<i>stem</i>]; applied to a plant. (Ibn-Abbád, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
And (assumed tropical:)  The <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَلْع</span> [or <i>spadix</i>] <i>of a palm-tree, when
it has come forth, and become a span in length.</i>
(K.)

